  "abstract": "This paper formulates a projection-first dark-sector hypothesis within Modal Triplet Theory (MTT) and identifies exactly what would be required to turn it into a physical model. The retained idea is that a reduced description may have an availability profile in which statistical or relational encodings remain usable while more local encodings do not. We prove, however, that an availability profile alone cannot determine a stress-energy tensor, a modified field equation, an equation of state, or a perturbation spectrum. In particular, statistical encoding does not imply cold, pressureless, collisionless matter, and relational encoding does not imply accelerated expansion. We replace the former identification of dark matter with E9 and dark energy with E8 by two explicit hypotheses. Each requires a selected covariant source map or a selected diffeomorphism-invariant effective action. We derive the associated conservation condition and state separate background, linear-perturbation, lensing, cluster-collision, cosmic-microwave-background, baryon-acoustic-oscillation, structure-growth, and equation-of-state gates. The current MTT result is consequently an organized candidate taxonomy and a completion contract, not a derivation of the observed dark sector.",
